          "w": "640"
        },
        "parms": "# mpeconfig, mpeformat and mpeparse — MPE\nMPE, MIDI Polyphonic Expression, gives each sounding note its own MIDI channel, so pitch bend, pressure and slide can move one note of a chord. A zone has a master channel, whose messages apply to every note, and member channels, one per note. In the lower zone the master is channel 1 and the members count up from 2. mpeconfig tells a device how many member channels there are, mpeformat builds MPE messages as byte lists for midiout, and mpeparse reads them back.\nMax's MPE objects can place up to seven zones anywhere and trade in mpeevent messages for poly~. Here there are the two zones MPE defines, lower (argument 0) and upper (1), and the member channel is what a note is known by. mpeparse reports only the MPE messages: wire midiparse to the same source for the rest.",
        "type": ".text"
      },
