        },
        "parms": "1. Click 15: mpeconfig 0 builds the configuration message for the lower zone, three controller messages on channel 1, and midiout sends them. The list box shows the last, 176 6 15: 15 member channels. A device that receives it sets the member channels' bend range to 48 semitones. 7 leaves channels 9 to 16 for ordinary MIDI, and 0 switches MPE off.",
        "type": ".text"
      },
      "object 32": {
        "ID": 32,
        "gui": {
          "x": "640.0",
          "y": "470.0",
          "w": "300"
        },
        "parms": "2. mpeformat plays on the member channel its right inlet stores: click 2. The button above pack 60 100 plays middle C on channel 2, 145 60 100. 8363 bends that note up about a semitone at the 48-semitone range, as the full 14 bits, and 8192 is the bend at rest. 90 presses the note, and 30 slides it, controller 74. Click 3 and the button above pack 64 90: E on channel 3, with a bend of its own. A pitch alone, 60 or 64, releases a note: click its channel first.",
        "type": ".text"
      },
      "object 33": {
        "ID": 33,
        "gui": {
          "x": "640.0",
          "y": "700.0",
          "w": "300"
        },
        "parms": "3. midiout opens its port when the first message arrives, and that first message is lost. So loadbang sends allnotesoff as the patch opens, and the port is ready before you click.",
        "type": ".text"
      },
      "object 34": {
        "ID": 34,
        "gui": {
          "x": "640.0",
          "y": "830.0",
          "w": "300"
        },
        "parms": "4. mpeparse reads what arrives on input port 0, through midiin. Left to right: the note as pitch and velocity, the bend, the pressure, the slide, the channel, and its role: 1 for a member channel, 2 for the master, 0 outside the zone. On Linux, output 0 and input 0 are usually Midi Through, which sends back whatever it receives, so mpeparse reads what you play here. With an MPE controller, set midiin's argument to its port.",
        "type": ".text"
      },
